{
  "mn13:0.1": "Middle Discourses 13 ",
  "mn13:0.2": "The Longer Discourse on the Mass of Suffering ",
  "mn13:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn13:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn13:2.1": "Then several mendicants robed up in the morning and, taking their bowls and robes, entered Sāvatthī for alms. ",
  "mn13:2.2": "Then it occurred to them, ",
  "mn13:2.3": "“It’s too early to wander for alms in Sāvatthī. ",
  "mn13:2.4": "Why don’t we visit the monastery for the wanderers of other religions?” ",
  "mn13:2.5": "Then they went to the monastery for the wanderers of other religions and exchanged greetings with the wanderers there. ",
  "mn13:2.6": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, they sat down to one side. The wanderers said to them: ",
  "mn13:3.1": "“Reverends, the ascetic Gotama advocates the complete understanding of sensual pleasures, and so do we. ",
  "mn13:3.2": "The ascetic Gotama advocates the complete understanding of forms, and so do we. ",
  "mn13:3.3": "The ascetic Gotama advocates the complete understanding of feelings, and so do we. ",
  "mn13:3.4": "What, then, is the difference between the ascetic Gotama’s teaching and instruction and ours?” ",
  "mn13:3.5": "",
  "mn13:4.1": "Those mendicants neither approved nor rejected that statement of the wanderers of other religions. ",
  "mn13:4.2": "They rose from their seats, thinking, ",
  "mn13:4.3": "“We will learn the mea